Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:33:55 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/33] sysfs: set up linear arrays from external metadata

sysfs_set_array() returns early for every level below 0, so for a linear
member array of an external container (DDF CONCAT, AMD Volume) neither
level nor raid_disks are written.  The kernel then refuses every slot,
as it is not below raid_disks (0), and such an array can be neither
created nor assembled:

  mdadm: failed to write '0' to '/sys/block/md126/md/dev-loop1/slot' (No space left on device)
  mdadm: ADD_NEW_DISK for /dev/md/ddf failed: No space left on device

Let linear arrays through, as the levels >= 0 are.  A DDF CONCAT is then
created, assembled and started, given a kernel with md linear (6.14 and
later).

Written by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model by Anthropic.
---
 sysfs.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sysfs.c b/sysfs.c
index 8fca3c01..2597fb02 100644
--- a/sysfs.c
+++ b/sysfs.c
@@ -987,7 +987,8 @@ int sysfs_set_array(struct mdinfo *info)
 			return 1;
 		}
 	}
-	if (info->array.level < 0)
+	/* linear (DDF CONCAT, AMD Volume) needs level and raid_disks too */
+	if (info->array.level < 0 && info->array.level != LEVEL_LINEAR)
 		return 0; /* FIXME */
 	rv |= sysfs_set_str(info, NULL, "level",
 			    map_num_s(pers, info->array.level));
